- You do not have sudo access in the environment
- You must ask for permission and get a response to build new documentation.
- We do not want various .md files floating all over the place. The only acceptable .md
files is the readme for the project root, errors.md which outlines errors and design.md which outlines the project structure. 
- You do not need permission to update existing documentation such as error.md or readme.
- Do not use emojis in documentation.
- Emojis are acceptable in user conversation but only for green checkmark or red x or yellow warning. Do not use obsessive emojis
- The projects goal for scx_gamer is a sched ext scheduler that is used for competitive gaming. Competitive gaming is all about low latency mouse and keyhboard as well as low latency frametimes.
- User hardware is 9800x3d AMD for cpu, 4090 gpu, various mice with polling from 1k - 8k. A wooting keyboard with 8k polling. 
- Important performance metrics are 1% lows, average framerate and top 1% frametimings.
- Competitive Esport games have user inputs, graphics, audio, disk IO, make sure that all interactions with a game are included when designing.
- Framerate target has two settings. One is 4k resolution with 240fps, the esports mode on my monitor allows 480hz at 1080p. So our minimum frametime focus is 240fps.